"""Sandboxes: containers Workpeg AI drives on somebody's behalf.

Nothing in this package is reachable from a live path. It is the seam
(:mod:`workpeg.sandbox.driver`) and its first backend
(:mod:`workpeg.sandbox.docker_driver`); the model, the endpoints, the compose
service and the reaper are all elsewhere and none of them call this yet.

The seam exists so "Docker now, a microVM later" is a swap rather than a
migration, and so the hardening lives in one place that every backend must
satisfy. Read :mod:`workpeg.sandbox.driver` first — it explains what a caller
is *not* allowed to choose, which is most of the design, and why the one
thing a caller *does* choose (``argv``) is a list and never a string.
"""
